{
  "quest.7A14E14A72F0C88F.title": "&2Bait",
  "quest.29C505C5D1927614.title": "&cInstant Health",
  "task.0530149F4E3FF764.title": "Kitchen Cabinets",
  "quest.6F6671705176E2F8.title": "&cRedstone Dust",
  "task.0637AC7B02D2E783.title": "Any Wood or Terracotta &aPlanter&r",
  "quest.47C84A22986E6A81.title": "&fToaster and Coffee",
  "quest.53C1013488EFFDED.title": "&2The Animal Trap",
  "quest.67647369B6065EEC.title": "&fHeating Unit",
  "quest.4DE0274AAFD9BF94.title": "&6Drying and Crushing",
  "quest.6E5692E47F7A4283.title": "&2Cloche Domes",
  "quest.23FFD172C3555282.title": "&fIndustrial Cooking",
  "quest.154E08BC9091684F.quest_desc": [
    "&aGlowstone Dust&r is used as an amplifier for potions effects.",
    "",
    "When added, this will usually increase the strength of the potion.",
  ],
  "quest.19DB27ECAB774058.quest_desc": [
    "Watch the bobber and strike at the right moment. That is only the start; once a fish is on, it fights.",
    "",
    "Reeling one in means hitting its &asweetspots&r as they appear, and they are not all the same:",
    "",
    "- &fBasic&r: the standard one, straightforward progress.",
    "- &7Stone&r: barely awards any progress at all.",
    "- &bFrozen&r: avoid it entirely.",
    "- &7Deepslate&r: disappears if you are too slow.",
    "- &6Gold&r: awards treasure progress rather than catch progress.",
    "",
    "&aDifferent species fight differently&r, so knowing what you have hooked is half the battle. The guide tells you before you cast.",
    "",
    "There is a playtest mode in the guide's settings if you want to practice without losing a catch.",
  ],
  "quest.53C1013488EFFDED.quest_desc": [
    "The &aAnimal Trap&r needs bait, and the bait decides what it catches. Wheat seeds bring a chicken and a carrot brings a pig. JEI's Trapping tab lists the rest.",
    "",
    "After a short wait it rolls a &a5% chance every second&r. A caught animal stays in the trap and drops its loot every two and a half minutes for as long as you keep it baited, and each drop has a 10% chance to use up one bait.",
    "",
    "&aWaterlog it&r and bait it with kelp in a river or ocean and it catches salmon instead.",
  ],
  "quest.67647369B6065EEC.quest_desc": [
    "Add the &cHeating Upgrade&r to a Stove to allow you to use Power to cook items instead of using Coal!",
  ],
  "quest.487F2399A124C3E8.quest_desc": [
    "A pasture full of cows is a lot of animals for the game to track. An &aAnimal Pen&r keeps a whole herd in one block.",
    "",
    "Right-click an untamed adult animal with an &aAnimal Cage&r to catch it, then right-click the pen with the cage to put it inside. Sneak and right-click the pen with an empty cage to take half of them back out.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Feed the pen the animal's usual breeding food to grow the herd, up to &a24&r animals. A bucket takes milk from cows and eggs from chickens, shears take wool from sheep, and a sword or axe harvests the animals for their drops.",
    "",
    "Pens also work with comparators and dispensers, so the milking and shearing can be automated.",
  ],
  "quest.3AAE0A3262894C43.quest_desc": [
    "&aCapacitors&r store the &cRF&r your burners make and hand it out to everything nearby.",
    "",
    "They need no setup at all. They balance their own charge between themselves automatically, so you drop a few around the farm and stop thinking about it.",
    "",
    "Three tiers, each holding more and transferring faster than the last.",
  ],
  "quest.18DEFD2E007D08AA.title": "&2Orchards and Bushes",
  "quest.11C072E618300154.title": "&6Treasure Fishing",
  "quest.186BE7F6DFA8C41E.quest_desc": [
    "&3Gunpowder&r converts potions into &aSplash Potions&r.",
    "",
    "These potions are instead thrown for an AoE effect, rather than drinking them straight.",
  ],
  "quest.586A4F3BBC9F7275.title": "&fClams and Pearls",
  "quest.46223192C9DD4975.title": "&fConnectors and Chicken Sinks",
  "quest.5D2D114B66DE61EE.title": "&bInfinite Water Source?",
  "quest.10AB0C0930A5D77D.title": "&5Regeneration",
  "quest.4498067DF133EEFD.title": "&aAviaries",
  "quest.0F15A94920C420AC.title": "&6The Horse Powered Generator",
  "quest.3A389EDA045B65E1.quest_desc": [
    "Carrots come out of village farms and off the occasional zombie. One is enough to start a plot of your own.",
    "",
    "They grow on tilled, watered farmland and take light like any crop. Replant from what you harvest and the plot pays for itself in a night.",
  ],
  "quest.3257746A213CB9B7.title": "&6Tournaments and Trophies",
  "quest.42B3EE6283C80A80.quest_desc": [
    "A &aHorse Press&r squeezes seeds into &2Seed Oil&r. It also presses flowers into dye and ice into water, and JEI's Horse Pressing tab lists the rest.",
    "",
    "Seed Oil is furnace fuel, and one bucket burns long enough to smelt 80 items. That turns the leftover seeds from any farm into something worth having.",
    "",
    "It is stored and moved as a fluid, so it needs a bucket or a tank.",
  ],
  "quest.287E6819DB849CD4.quest_desc": [
    "The &aTool Rack&r is a perfect place to store your cooking utensils for retrieval.",
    "",
    "It also makes your kitchen look more like a kitchen!",
  ],
  "quest.10BE7DAF2BEAF714.title": "&fCookie and Milk Jars",
  "quest.3879EE0C19E79053.quest_desc": [
    "The &aHorse Chopper&r is the powered version of the chopping block. It stands two blocks tall, so it needs a free block of space above wherever you place it.",
    "",
    "It turns logs into planks and some wooden items back into sticks, far faster than chopping by hand.",
    "",
    "The animal walks a 7 by 7 ring around the machine. Only two solid blocks such as chests or hoppers are allowed inside that ring, so keep the path clear.",
  ],
  "quest.6D8485CEF00C0B60.quest_desc": [
    "Fourteen new crops, each with its own seeds, from &aCorn&r and Cauliflower to rice, soybeans and strawberries. JEI lists them all.",
    "",
    "Your first seeds come from chest loot, the Farmer's &aMarket&r or a wandering trader. After that the Artisan Press turns a crop back into seeds.",
    "",
    "They grow on ordinary farmland. The Agritech planters have no recipes for them, so plant these in the ground.",
  ],
  "quest.42B3EE6283C80A80.title": "&6The Horse Press",
  "quest.0F15A94920C420AC.quest_desc": [
    "The bridge to everything else in this pack is a generator that runs on &aa walking animal&r.",
    "",
    "It makes 80 FE/t, and only while it gets a redstone signal, so put a lever on it. It will never keep up with a reactor, but it will run your first machine before you have any other way to make energy at all.",
    "",
    "&7&oIf you are starting a fresh world, this is a genuinely viable first power source.&r",
  ],
  "quest.1E0BB50868F951A3.title": "&fFruit Basket",
  "quest.514E3A822BFB730B.title": "&fFree Milk!",
  "quest.553EE7D5FF66C61D.title": "&6The Tackle Box",
  "quest.2EA7CCDB687AC468.quest_desc": [
    "The &aPreservation Upgrade&r will always try to keep at least 1 item from a stack from being used up in recipes.",
  ],
  "task.3B7699715021E7F7.title": "Placed Foods",
  "quest.6B7CE7931C91B128.title": "&2Spreaders and Silos",
  "quest.3A11543E54EFD7D9.title": "&2Biomass and Power",
  "quest.709DACF3C4655662.title": "&fThe Pantry",
  "quest.553EE7D5FF66C61D.quest_desc": [
    "The &aTackle Box&r stores your catch and every piece of fishing gear, and it is the only place you can swap what is attached to your rod.",
    "",
    "Three attachment slots, each changing how fishing behaves:",
    "",
    "- &aHooks&r: Iron, Stone, Copper (through all its oxidation stages), Gold, Amethyst, Frozen, Echoing, Heavy, Mossy, Rusty, Shiny, Split and Vanilla-flavoured.",
    "- &2Bobbers&r: the plain Bobber, Steady, Clear, Leafy, Slimey, Dripstone, Glowing, Golden, Cloud and Vanilla-flavoured.",
    "- &aBaits&r: see the next quest.",
    "",
    "Fisherman's Hats carry modifiers too, and turn up rarely in shipwreck chests.",
  ],
  "quest.2EA7CCDB687AC468.title": "&fPreservation Unit",
  "quest.73846333D68F6339.title": "&fPotato Farm",
  "quest.52F610F471E53EFB.title": "&2The Advanced Planter",
  "quest.487F2399A124C3E8.title": "&aAnimal Pens",
  "quest.7B3B55130DE2D019.title": "&6The Artisan Press",
  "quest.5D2D114B66DE61EE.quest_desc": [
    "Whether you are washing dishes or powering nuclear reactors, the &aKitchen Sink&r provides easy access to an infinite source of water.",
    "",
    "When connected to the &bKitchen Multiblock&r, this will provide access to recipes that require Water.",
  ],
  "quest.24E11CBBB6EC58D5.title": "&fBlaze Powder",
  "quest.3670FA7818A11284.quest_desc": [
    "There are plenty of great foods out there that provide great stats, but nothing can replace the benefits from &cBrewing Potions&r.",
    "",
    "You'll need to borrow a &cBlaze Rod&r from a Blaze first, or just steal a stand from your local sky village.",
    "",
    "&7&oWho am I to judge?",
  ],
  "quest.014A81275259E6AF.quest_desc": [
    "The first real machine. Hitch a saddled animal to a &aHorse Grindstone&r and it turns without you.",
    "",
    "Grinding gives you &aFlour&r, which becomes &2Dough&r and then bread, and it handles ore and other materials besides.",
    "",
    "A Wooden Hopper feeds it, so the whole thing can run unattended once it is set up.",
  ],
  "quest.5DBBF2E8AEFB4149.title": "&6Pantry for Blockheads",
  "quest.02B468BF096A840A.title": "&aTraits on &5Essence Crops",
  "quest.19DB27ECAB774058.title": "&bThe Sweetspot Minigame",
  "quest.73846333D68F6339.quest_desc": [
    "Same story as carrots, same places to find the first one.",
    "",
    "Potatoes are the better bulk crop because baking them is a furnace job rather than a recipe, and a baked potato feeds you properly.",
  ],
  "quest.073546F80EDA632E.title": "&fThe &aMarket",
  "quest.15441C87BEDC510C.title": "&2Agritech Evolved",
  "quest.2545259D5B8A6139.title": "&2Other Crops",
  "quest.186BE7F6DFA8C41E.title": "&7Gunpowder",
  "quest.6E5692E47F7A4283.quest_desc": [
    "A &aCloche Dome&r sits on top of a &2Planter&r and raises both growth speed and yield.",
    "",
    "It &astacks&r with fertilizer and with whatever soil you've used, so a planter running &2Infused Farmland&r under a dome and fed by a spreader is about as fast as this mod gets.",
    "",
    "Sneak + Right-click with an empty hand to take a dome back off.",
  ],
  "quest.3C972EE25114E1AE.title": "&6Horse Powered",
  "quest.4C50A70027F208BE.quest_desc": [
    "Not all foods are eaten in your hands.",
    "",
    "Foods like &aCake&r will need to be placed down first, but will provide multiple slices to replenish your hunger!",
  ],
  "quest.79CC3BBEC8B16640.quest_desc": [
    "The &aFridge&r is the perfect place to store cold items, and can be upgraded to provide more recipes for your &bKitchen Multiblock&r!",
  ],
  "quest.59BFB93E613911CD.quest_desc": [
    "A &aNetherite&r upgrade at the smithing table lets your rod fish in lava. Until then an &dAmethyst Hook&r does the same job on any rod.",
    "",
    "The other named rods (Bamboo, Boner, Humble, Naturalist, Sky, Obsidian, Iceborn, Magmaforged, Slimed, Sharktooth, Lush Glowberry and Azure Crystal) are skins, not upgrades. Each comes from a &aSkin Smithing Template&r, and applying one changes how your rod looks while it keeps everything attached to it.",
    "",
    "&7&oAll the Nether species bite in lava, and so do a few in Overworld lava lakes.",
  ],
  "quest.7A14E14A72F0C88F.quest_desc": [
    "&aWorms&r are the starting bait and you get them by &2bonemealing farmland&r, which makes them effectively free.",
    "",
    "&aUse a bucket as bait&r and you pull up the bucketed version of whatever you catch.",
    "",
    "Only a few catches demand one specific bait, and the guide marks them. A &aCreeper Head&r wants Gunpowder Bait, and a Nether Star wants a Wither Skeleton Skull.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Most baits cut your lure time, but several do more than that:",
    "",
    "- &aAlmighty Worm&r: lets you catch certain fish alive.",
    "- &2Seeking Worm&r: makes species you have not caught yet more likely to bite.",
    "- &aLegendary Bait&r: the shortest wait for a bite of any bait.",
    "- &2Meteorological Bait&r: fish that only bite at a certain time of day or in certain weather will bite anyway.",
    "- &aThemed baits&r: Cherry, Dripstone, Gunpowder, Lush, Murkwater and Sculk Bait cut the wait exactly like a Worm.",
  ],
  "quest.72EAA9618A3E114D.title": "&5Tiered Essence Soils",
  "quest.31BD9A98AE5893B9.quest_desc": [
    "Everyone has a &aSpice Rack&r in their kitchen.",
    "",
    "If you don't, what is going on in your kitchen?",
  ],
  "task.32F204C4D02EF945.title": "Any #starcatcher:bobbers",
  "quest.18DEFD2E007D08AA.quest_desc": [
    "The mod also plants things in the world: &aLemon&r and &2Peach&r trees, Blueberry bushes and Grape vines, all generating in the biomes tagged for them.",
    "",
    "Two smaller touches worth knowing:",
    "- &aSweet Berry Bushes no longer slow or damage you.",
    "- &2Overeating grants a Well Fed absorption effect&r on certain foods.",
    "",
    "Fortune Cookies give a random effect on a cooldown, and there are three dozen different fortunes to read.",
  ],
  "quest.0800E48C01F45F46.title": "&fSweet Berry Farm",
  "quest.1A64C6CE416B7C5E.quest_desc": [
    "This pack runs three fishing systems at once, and they stack rather than conflict.",
    "",
    "- &bStarcatcher&r replaces what you catch and adds the sweetspot fight.",
    "- &3Nautec's Lucky Zones&r are patches of water that add an extra loot roll wherever you cast into them. &aAny rod works&r, including a Starcatcher's Rod.",
    "- &6Little Joys Fishing Spots&r are bubble patches that do much the same thing, from a third mod entirely.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "&aThe Prismatic Fishing Rod&r has its own strike minigame, separate from Starcatcher's sweetspots. Each bite picks a timing bar, a three-tap rhythm or a hold at random. You will want to pick one rod and learn its rhythm rather than switching constantly.",
    "",
    "The Nautec Lucky Zones quest is linked onto this board so you can read it without leaving the chapter.",
  ],
  "quest.10963E2F6AEC9B3B.title": "&2Upgrade Modules",
  "quest.4B4358B6B25DC413.quest_desc": [
    "&eStarcatcher&r adds its own fishing alongside the vanilla kind. A vanilla Fishing Rod still pulls the normal vanilla catches, and the first time you catch something with one you also fish up a &aStarcatcher's Rod&r and the &2Starcatcher's Guide&r.",
    "",
    "Everything new needs the &aStarcatcher's Rod&r. Over a hundred species are spread across biomes, dimensions and weather conditions.",
    "",
    "The &aStarcatcher's Guide&r shows where each fish lives, what bait it wants and how hard it fights. An entry stays hidden until you have caught that fish once.",
  ],
  "quest.10BE7DAF2BEAF714.quest_desc": [
    "Two small storage blocks for the kitchen.",
    "",
    "Right-click the &aCookie Jar&r to open its five slots. Anything inside counts as kitchen storage, so the Cooking Table can use it.",
    "",
    "The &aMilk Jar&r holds milk for recipes. Right-click it with a Milk Bucket to fill it, or with an empty bucket to take a bucket back out.",
    "",
    "A Milk Jar is also what you squash a cow onto to make a &aCow in a Jar&r, so build a spare.",
  ],
  "quest.287E6819DB849CD4.title": "&fTool Rack",
  "quest.764201B687CCFD38.title": "&aAquariums",
  "quest.4145FED51D1ACD76.quest_desc": [
    "Nether wart is the base of nearly every potion, and every stack you will ever brew starts with one found in a fortress or a bastion.",
    "",
    "Back home it grows on &aSoul Sand&r, needs no water and no light, and does not care which dimension it sits in. Bring soul sand back with the wart.",
  ],
  "quest.0800E48C01F45F46.quest_desc": [
    "Sweet berry bushes grow wild in taiga. Break one and you keep the bush, so a single trip stocks a whole row at home.",
    "",
    "They plant on grass or dirt without tilling, which makes them the least demanding food in the pack. Pantry for Blockheads also stops the bushes from hurting or slowing you, so you can walk straight through a row.",
  ],
  "quest.31BD9A98AE5893B9.title": "&fSpice Rack",
  "quest.5DBBF2E8AEFB4149.quest_desc": [
    "&ePantry for Blockheads&r is the food half of the Blockheads family, and it is large, close to a hundred ingredients and prepared dishes.",
    "",
    "This chapter covers the parts you need to get going. For the food itself, &acheck JEI&r rather than a quest list.",
    "",
    "Three tools do most of the work:",
    "- &aChef's Knife&r for prep.",
    "- &2Frying Pan&r for anything cooked in one.",
    "- &aBaking Sheet&r for anything baked.",
    "",
    "They slot into the Cooking for Blockheads kitchen you already built.",
  ],
  "quest.709DACF3C4655662.quest_desc": [
    "I'm sure you have a ton of different items that you want to cook with, and you also don't want to spend all of your time searching up what to do with them in JEI.",
    "",
    "Shove everything into a &aKitchen Counter&r or &2Cabinet&r! As long as it is connected to the &bKitchen Multiblock&r, you can access most of the recipes for them using the Cooking Table.",
  ],
  "quest.014A81275259E6AF.title": "&6The Horse Grindstone",
  "quest.79CC3BBEC8B16640.title": "&fFridges",
  "quest.29C505C5D1927614.quest_desc": [
    "The first potion worth carrying. Brew &aNether Wart&r into a water bottle for an &2Awkward Potion&r, then add a Glistering Melon Slice.",
    "",
    "It heals the moment you drink it rather than over time, which is the difference between surviving a bad fight and reading the death screen.",
    "",
    "Add &aGlowstone Dust&r to make it heal harder, or &2Gunpowder&r to throw it at someone else.",
  ],
  "quest.4498067DF133EEFD.quest_desc": [
    "Flying animals go in an &aAviary&r, caught with an &2Avian Net&r.",
    "",
    "Bees are the ones worth keeping. Feed them a small flower to breed them, and they build up pollen over time. Shears harvest it as honeycomb, and a glass bottle takes it as honey.",
    "",
    "&7&oParrots, bats and allays are only decorative in here, though an allay fed an amethyst shard duplicates.&r",
  ],
  "quest.4B4358B6B25DC413.title": "&bStarcatcher",
  "quest.46223192C9DD4975.quest_desc": [
    "A kitchen only counts as one kitchen if its blocks touch. Fill a gap or turn a corner between two runs of counters with &aKitchen Connectors&r. For a gap you need to walk through, lay &2Kitchen Floor&r tiles instead, which link the kitchen through the floor.",
    "",
    "The &aChicken Sink&r is a coop, not a water source. Right-click it with an Egg and the egg hatches after 10 minutes. The chick needs seeds in the sink's feed slot to grow up, and the grown chicken lays eggs that kitchen recipes can use.",
    "",
    "Counters, cabinets, sinks, chicken sinks, ovens, fridges, cooking tables and connectors all come in the sixteen dye colors if you care what your kitchen looks like.",
  ],
  "quest.3257746A213CB9B7.quest_desc": [
    "The &aTournament Stand&r runs fishing competitions, and the &2Fish Radar&r tells you what is available where you are standing.",
    "",
    "Trophies come in &6Copper&r, &fIron&f, Gold, &bDiamond&r and &aEmerald&r, and then there is the &6Trophy Of The Older Angler&r for whoever finishes the collection.",
    "",
    "&7&oEating Starcaught Fish leaves Fish Bones behind, which have their own uses.&r",
  ],
  "quest.7B3B55130DE2D019.quest_desc": [
    "The mod's workstation, and the one block you actually need to build.",
    "",
    "&7&oCheck JEI on the Artisan Press to see everything it makes.&r",
  ],
  "quest.7D090A60681CC97D.quest_desc": [
    "The &aCooking Table&r is the first big craft you'll want to make to get started making your kitchen!",
    "",
    "This block acts as the main crafting table for foods, and is the centerpiece of your &aKitchen Multiblock&r. When opened, it will show you every food you can make based on what you have stored in the multiblock and what appliances you have connected.",
    "",
    "Note: Certain mods won't connect with it, like the &bFarmer's Delight Cooking Pot&r. Make sure to always check JEI for specific recipes! ",
  ],
  "quest.35865030C4D59D8C.title": "&bIce Unit",
  "quest.3A11543E54EFD7D9.quest_desc": [
    "Farming produces waste, and &eAgritech&r burns it.",
    "",
    "&aCrude Biomass&r is the starter fuel and it is, in the mod's own words, very inefficient. Real &2Biomass&r only comes out of the &aComposter&r from the Compost and Mulch quest. Compact it into Compacted Biomass and then a Compacted Biomass Block, and each step holds more energy than the last.",
    "",
    "The &aBiomass Burner&r turns any of them into &cRF&r, which is what runs the rest of the machinery. A farm that powers itself off its own clippings is the whole idea.",
  ],
  "quest.6D8485CEF00C0B60.title": "&2Blockhead Crops",
  "quest.308D28C1370CED08.quest_desc": [
    "The &aComposter&r turns plant scraps into &2Biomass&r. It takes anything a vanilla composter accepts, and it runs faster on power but still works without it.",
    "",
    "Biomass compacts down into the ingredients for &aMulch&r. In a Planter's soil slot, Mulch grants &a50%&r growth speed to flowers, saplings, mushrooms and anything else that grows on dirt.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Crops that need farmland will not accept plain Mulch. Right-click it in the planter with a &2Hoe&r and it becomes &aInfused Farmland&r, which doubles that to &a100%&r and also works out in the world as ordinary farmland.",
    "",
    "It is also the one soil every &eMystical Agriculture&r essence seed accepts. Plain Farmland in a planter only grows tier 1 essence seeds, so if a seed refuses to go in, this is the block that fixes it.",
  ],
  "quest.308D28C1370CED08.title": "&aCompost, Mulch and Infused Farmland",
  "quest.6B7CE7931C91B128.quest_desc": [
    "This is where the farm stops needing you.",
    "",
    "The &aFertilizer Spreader&r fertilizes every planter in range on its own, and the &2Silo&r collects the harvest from them and holds it.",
    "",
    "Both work on a radius, so the layout question becomes how many planters you can fit inside one spreader's reach.",
  ],
  "quest.1E0BB50868F951A3.quest_desc": [
    "The &aFruit Basket&r is essentially just another storage block for your &bKitchen Multiblock&r, but it can visually store &2Fruits&r!",
  ],
  "quest.6BDDB9A4E1E30213.quest_desc": [
    "You do not need an animal to start. Two blocks work on elbow grease alone:",
    "",
    "- &aHand Grindstone&r grinds without a horse.",
    "- &2Chopping Block&r chops without one either.",
    "",
    "They are slower than the powered versions and they need you standing there, but they cost almost nothing and work from your first day.",
    "",
    "JEI lists Manual Grinding and Manual Chopping as separate categories from the horse-powered ones. Check both.",
  ],
  "quest.52F610F471E53EFB.quest_desc": [
    "The &aAdvanced Planter&r grows crops twice as fast as the basic one, and it has two module slots for Speed and Yield upgrades, which the basic planter lacks.",
    "",
    "It runs on power. It draws &c128 RF/t&r while it works and stops when the power runs out, so keep it next to a &aCapacitor&r.",
  ],
  "quest.073546F80EDA632E.quest_desc": [
    "Need a specific seed for your farm? Check out the local Farmer's &aMarket&r!",
    "",
    "Once placed, this will call a local Farmer that sells most seeds and items needed for a great farm.",
    "",
    "The &aMarket&r saves a lot of wandering when you need a crop you haven't found yet.",
    "{image:minecraft:item/emerald width:20 height:20 align:center}",
  ],
  "quest.72EAA9618A3E114D.quest_desc": [
    "The catch is soil tier. Each essence seed needs a soil matching its tier, so a &5Tier 1&r seed will grow in a planter a &dTier 5&r seed refuses.",
    "",
    "As you climb the &5Inferium &r&f→&f&d Prudentium &r&f→&f Tertium &f→&f Imperium &f→&f Supremium ladder you'll need to keep the farming soil climbing with it.",
    "",
    "Planters also drop &5Fertilized Essence&r alongside the crop, and return the seed itself now and then, so a planted essence farm slowly pays for its own expansion.",
    "",
    "Check JEI on any essence seed to see which soil tier it needs.",
  ],
  "quest.764201B687CCFD38.quest_desc": [
    "The &aAquatic Jar&r and the &2Aquariums&r do the same job for fish, squid and dolphins.",
    "",
    "Catch them with the jar and fill the aquarium the same way you fill a pen. Fish breed on seagrass or kelp, and squid and dolphins on any fish.",
    "",
    "A sword or axe harvests them, and a water bucket scoops a fish out to keep.",
  ],
  "quest.4DE0274AAFD9BF94.quest_desc": [
    "Two more blocks that work without an animal.",
    "",
    "- &aDrying Rack&r: dries what you put on it over time. Jade shows the progress and how much time is left.",
    "- &aGranite Anvil&r: a manual crusher. Put a block on it and strike it with a pickaxe to break stone into cobblestone, cobblestone into gravel and gravel into sand.",
    "",
    "Flint and Tinder is the mod's answer to needing fire before you have iron.",
  ],
  "quest.3AAE0A3262894C43.title": "&2Capacitors",
  "task.1DBF06AF493A4F76.title": "Any &aAnimal Pen&r",
  "quest.02B468BF096A840A.quest_desc": [
    "The second half of the compatibility story.",
    "",
    "&eProductive Farming&r applies its trait system to &eMystical Agriculture&r crops as well as its own. Essence crops can carry Growth, Yield, Resistance and Mutability just like corn. Each time one reaches a new growth stage it has a chance to raise a trait, 6% for a tier 1 seed down to 1% for tier 6.",
    "",
    "Pollen does nothing on essence crops, since none of them has a mutation. Raise a &cVery High&r yield &5Inferium&r strain by replanting seeds from your best plants as their traits climb. Then grow it in an &eAgritech&r planter on &2Infused Farmland&r under a &aCloche Dome&r and collect it with a Silo.",
    "",
    "&7&oThree mods, one essence farm, and no part of it needs you standing there.&r",
  ],
  "quest.23FFD172C3555282.quest_desc": [
    "When connected to the &bKitchen Multiblock&r, the &aStove&r will provide access to recipes that require the use of a furnace or smoker as long as it has fuel.",
    "",
    "This appliance will cook up to 9 items at the same time!",
  ],
  "quest.11C072E618300154.quest_desc": [
    "Sometimes something considerably heavier pulls on the hook. That is &6treasure&r.",
    "",
    "Getting it means working the &6gold sweetspots&r while still reeling in the fish itself, so it is a harder fight for a better reward. Most treasure is a roll on the vanilla fishing treasure table, but a few rare species carry a smithing template for a rod or tackle skin instead.",
    "",
    "A &aMessage in a Bottle&r is not treasure. It is a catch of its own, and each message can only be caught once. The first ones turn up at y 50 or higher once you have caught 10 rare fish. Others need 15 rare or 10 epic catches, a legendary catch and surface lava, or a Wither Skeleton Skull as bait.",
    "",
    "&7&oGreed costs catches. You can lose both if you push a fight too far.&r",
  ],
  "quest.3A389EDA045B65E1.title": "&fCarrot Farm",
  "quest.1A64C6CE416B7C5E.title": "&dThree Fishing Systems",
  "quest.2545259D5B8A6139.quest_desc": [
    "Five more vanilla crops are worth a spot on the farm, and none of them needs a quest of its own.",
    "",
    "- &aBeetroot&r grows like wheat, from seeds found in village farms and chests.",
    "- &2Pumpkins&r and &aMelons&r grow from stems, and the fruit appears on a free block of dirt, grass or farmland beside the stem, so leave room.",
    "- &aSugar Cane&r grows on dirt or sand next to water, up to three blocks tall. Break the top and leave the base.",
    "- &2Glow Berries&r come from cave vines in lush caves, and they grow down from the underside of a block.",
  ],
  "quest.7D090A60681CC97D.title": "&fBuilding Your Kitchen",
  "quest.10963E2F6AEC9B3B.quest_desc": [
    "Three families of module, three tiers each.",
    "",
    "- &aRange MK1/2/3&r extends the reach of a &2Silo&r or Fertilizer Spreader by 16, 32, or 64 blocks.",
    "- &aSpeed MK1/2/3&r makes machines work faster.",
    "- &2Yield MK1/2/3&r makes them produce more per harvest.",
    "",
    "&7&oA single MK3 range module turns one spreader into the whole farm's fertilizer supply",
  ],
  "quest.154E08BC9091684F.title": "&aGlowstone Dust",
  "quest.6BDDB9A4E1E30213.title": "&6Doing It By Hand",
  "quest.76F225C6B9A79620.quest_desc": [
    "To make any potion, you'll need to make an &aAwkward Potion&r first.",
    "",
    "This will give you a base to work with!",
  ],
  "quest.15441C87BEDC510C.quest_desc": [
    "&eAgritech Evolved&r is farming as machinery. Instead of tilling a field and walking it with a hoe, you build &aPlanters&r and let them do the growing.",
    "",
    "A &aPlanter&r holds soil and a crop. Right-click it with a &aHoe&r to till the soil you put inside, and right-click with &2Bone Meal&r or any fertilizer to push the growth along.",
    "",
    "Planters come in every wood type, so pick whichever matches the build you're putting it in.",
    "",
    "A planter also improves its own seed as it works. Before every harvest, the planted seed has a chance to raise one of its &eProductive Farming&r traits, 7% for most crops and 6% down to 1% for &eMystical Agriculture&r seeds. Growth makes the planter faster, Yield adds extra crops to each harvest, and any seeds it drops copy the planted seed's traits.",
  ],
  "quest.3C972EE25114E1AE.quest_desc": [
    "Before electricity, before steam, there was a horse walking in a circle.",
    "",
    "&eHorse Powered&r is early-game processing that needs no power at all. Every machine runs two ways. Work it &2by hand&r, slowly, or hitch an animal to it with a &aWork Saddle&r and let it do the work.",
    "",
    "It gives you flour, seed oil, planks, dried goods and a trickle of energy long before any tech mod will.",
    "",
    "[\"\", {\"text\": \"Grab the \", \"color\": \"gray\", \"italic\": true}, {\"text\": \"Horse Powered Guide\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"italic\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,horsepowered:guide,horsepowered:index.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Horse Powered Guide\"}}, {\"text\": \". It covers every machine and both operating modes.\", \"color\": \"gray\", \"italic\": true}]",
  ],
  "quest.67E0794BC2E568C1.quest_desc": [
    "The &aCutting Board&r is a flat crafting table. Right-click it for a normal 3x3 crafting grid.",
    "",
    "It does not join the kitchen network, so it cannot reach what your counters hold. Bring the ingredients with you.",
  ],
  "quest.76F225C6B9A79620.title": "&fAwkward Potion",
  "task.6CDD4C0D99BEAE16.title": "Any &aAviary&r",
  "quest.586A4F3BBC9F7275.quest_desc": [
    "Place a &aClam&r on sand and it slowly grows a &fPearl&f. Once it opens, click it to harvest.",
    "",
    "Pearls also rarely yield the &aPearl Tackle Smithing Template&r.",
  ],
  "quest.24E11CBBB6EC58D5.quest_desc": [
    "Blaze powder is what makes a &aBrewing Stand&r run, and it comes from blaze rods dropped in nether fortresses.",
    "",
    "One rod grinds into two powder, and one powder covers several brews. Bring back more rods than you think you need; half of them end up in eyes of ender instead.",
  ],
  "quest.59BFB93E613911CD.title": "&5Rods and Lava Fishing",
  "quest.3879EE0C19E79053.title": "&6The Horse Chopper",
  "quest.47C84A22986E6A81.quest_desc": [
    "Two appliances that work on their own, outside the kitchen network.",
    "",
    "Right-click the &aToaster&r with bread to load two slices, then right-click it with an empty hand to start it. A minute later they pop out as Toasted Bread. Toast them a second time and you get charcoal.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "It also toasts potatoes, kelp, chorus fruit, corn and snowballs, two at a time. It is slower than a furnace, but it never needs fuel.",
    "",
    "The &aCoffee Machine&r brews &2Coffee&r. Hold a Water Bottle, keep Cocoa Beans anywhere in your inventory, and right-click the machine. Each cup uses one bottle and one bean, and drinking it gives Haste and Speed for a minute and a half.",
    "",
    "Don't sneak while you click, or you drink the water instead.",
  ],
  "quest.4C50A70027F208BE.title": "&dTime For A Feast",
  "quest.6F6671705176E2F8.quest_desc": [
    "When added to potions, &cRedstone&r can be used to increase the duration of potion's effects.",
  ],
  "quest.4145FED51D1ACD76.title": "&fNether Wart",
  "quest.67E0794BC2E568C1.title": "&fThe Cutting Board",
  "quest.35865030C4D59D8C.quest_desc": [
    "The &bIce Upgrade&r can be added to a Fridge to provide Ice and Snow recipes to the &bKitchen Multiblock&r.",
  ],
  "task.5C621DC20ED224E0.title": "Kitchen Counters",
  "quest.3670FA7818A11284.title": "&fTime To &dBrew",
  "quest.514E3A822BFB730B.quest_desc": [
    "Lots of cooking recipes require &bMilk&r, and you won't want to run to your nearest Cow friend to grab some every time you need it.",
    "",
    "That's why you should just shove the &6Cow in a Jar&r. When added to the &bKitchen Multiblock&r, this will provide recipes with Milk Buckets if they call for it.",
    "",
    "But how do you get one? First, you need to make a &aMilk Jar&r. This can store milk by itself, but you'll want a renewable source of Milk for your kitchen.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Next, you'll need to place the Milk Jar in a hole that's big enough where a Cow can fit in.",
    "",
    "Lure a Cow into the hole where it is directly on top of the Milk Jar, then drop an Anvil into the hole. This will smoosh the Cow into the Jar!",
    "",
    "This will provide milk slowly over time for your Kitchen.",
  ],
  "quest.10AB0C0930A5D77D.quest_desc": [
    "Awkward Potion plus a &aGhast Tear&r. The tear is the hard part, and ghasts drop them over lava seas in the nether.",
    "",
    "Regeneration heals gradually instead of all at once, so it is the one to drink before a fight rather than during it. &aRedstone Dust&r stretches the duration.",
  ],
}